## The change

Vanilla 1.8.9 has no always-sprint; you double-tap W or hold the sprint key. I added a block in `EntityPlayerSP.onLivingUpdate()` that runs **after** vanilla's own sprint logic, so it wins over the stop condition:

```java
// Runs after the vanilla sprint checks above so it wins over the stop condition.
// The same guards vanilla uses are kept, otherwise this would sprint while
// sneaking, eating, blind, or on an empty hunger bar.
if (this.mc.gameSettings.alwaysSprint && !this.isSprinting() && !this.isSneaking()
    && this.movementInput.moveForward >= f && !this.isCollidedHorizontally
    && flag3 && !this.isUsingItem() && !this.isPotionActive(Potion.blindness))
{
    this.setSprinting(true);
}
```

Placement matters. Vanilla's stop check immediately above is:

```java
if (this.isSprinting() && (this.movementInput.moveForward < f || this.isCollidedHorizontally || !flag3))
```

Putting my block **before** it would just get undone a moment later. After it, the sprint survives.

I deliberately kept vanilla's guards rather than forcing sprint unconditionally — otherwise you'd walk into an empty hunger bar while sprinting, and moving backwards would look broken.

## Behaviour`alwaysSprint` defaults to **false**, persisted as `alwaysSprint` in `options.txt` (load, save, and `resetSettings` all wired).

```
/sprint        → toggle
/sprint on     → always sprint
/sprint off    → back to vanilla
```

Sprint starts when you hold forward at ≥0.8 move input. Still blocked while sneaking, eating, blind, running into a wall, or at ≤6 food — same as vanilla. Releasing forward stops it, so it's not a permanent sprint state.

## Commands now registered

`/fov`, `/bob`, `/sprint` — five classes in the jar, `BUILD SUCCESSFUL`, 0 errors, `META-INF` stripped, natives dir intact.

Untested at runtime. One thing to watch when you try it: because the check is `!this.isSprinting()`, sprint state is re-evaluated every tick from live input, so diagonal movement and jump-into-water should behave. But whether the feel matches what you want is a judgement I can't make from here.

