        private static Field field(String name) throws Exception { ... }
    }

    /** Puts the feature in a known idle state without going through the saving setters. */
    private static void begin() throws Exception
    {
        State.modeField().set(null, FreeLook.Mode.HOLD);
        ...
    }
```

Hmm, needs access to the mode field statically. Let me make `modeField()` a static helper.

Let me rewrite the whole State class plus add `begin()` as a static method on the test class, and replace `State.start();` with `begin();`.

Also remove unused imports: `Method`, `Modifier`, `InputStreamReader` used, `FileInputStream` used. `Method`/`Modifier` unused — javac won't error on unused imports with -nowarn. Fine, but let me drop them for cleanliness.

