So lines 239-545 are the persistence block (getConfigFile, reset, load, Presence, resetToDefaults, applySetting, parseBooleanOr, parseHexOr, parseIntOr, save, closeQuietly). I need to keep `parseHexOr` (used by ClientConfig and FpsCommand).

Replacement block (lines 239..545) → new content:

```java
    /**
     * The single config file in the game directory.
     *
     * <p>Kept as a method on each mod so the commands can name the file without knowing that
     * {@link ClientConfig} owns it.</p>
     */
    public static File getConfigFile()
    {
        return ClientConfig.getConfigFile();
    }

    /**
     * Restores every value to its default and rewrites the config file.
     *
     * <p>Public because {@code /fps reset} exposes it.</p>
     */
    public static void reset()
    {
        resetToDefaults();
        resetSmoothing();
        save();
    }

    /** Restores defaults in memory. Does not write the file; see {@link ClientConfig#load()}. */
    static void resetToDefaults()
    {
        enabled = false;
        mode = Mode.NORMAL;
        size = 1.0F;
        posX = 4;
        posY = 4;
        alpha = 255;
        autoColour = true;
        colour = 0xFFFFFF;
        shadow = true;
    }

    /**
     * Parses {@code #RRGGBB} or bare {@code RRGGBB}.
     *
     * @return the 0xRRGGBB value, or the fallback if the text is not exactly six hex digits
     */
    static int parseHexOr(String value, int fallback)
    {
        String text = value.trim();

        if (text.startsWith("#"))
        {
            text = text.substring(1);
        }

        if (text.length() != 6)
        {
            return fallback;
        }

        try
        {
            return Integer.parseInt(text, 16) & 0xFFFFFF;
        }
        catch (NumberFormatException exception)
        {
            return fallback;
        }
    }

    /** Writes the config file. Never throws. */
    public static void save()
    {
        ClientConfig.save();
    }
```

