8: /**
9:  * Free look: the camera swings off the player's body rotation while the bind is held, or
10:  * while a toggle is on, so you can aim sideways without turning your character.
11:  *
12:  * <p>Vanilla funnels every mouse-look update through {@code EntityPlayerSP.setAngles}, which
13:  * adds to the body rotation. That single call is where this class takes over: while free look
14:  * is active the deltas accumulate into private yaw/pitch offsets instead, and the body never
15:  * turns. {@code EntityRenderer.orientCamera} adds the offsets back onto the view, and
16:  * {@code EntityPlayerSP.getLook} adds them too so the crosshair, the block outline and block
17:  * breaking follow the camera rather than the body.</p>
18:  *
19:  * <p>The body rotation is deliberately never modified. That keeps walking direction, the
20:  * rendered player model, and the packets sent to the server all matching each other, which is
21:  * what makes this behave instead of just look different.</p>
22:  *
23:  * <p>{@link View} restricts free look to first person, third person, or both. When the current
24:  * view is not allowed the bind is ignored outright and any banked offset is dropped, so the
25:  * camera is always exactly where the view restriction says it should be.</p>
26:  *
27:  * <p>Settings are persisted in {@value ClientConfig#FILE_NAME} in the game directory, alongside
28:  * every other mod setting. The key itself is a plain vanilla key bind, so it appears under
29:  * Options &gt; Controls and is stored in options.txt.</p>
30:  */
31: public final class FreeLook
32: {
33:     /** How the bind turns free look on. */
34:     public enum Mode
35:     {
36:         /** Free look is on exactly while the key is down. */
37:         HOLD,
38:         /** Pressing the key flips free look until pressed again. */
39:         TOGGLE
40:     }
41: 
42:     /** Which camera view free look is allowed to work in. */
43:     public enum View
44:     {
45:         /** Both first and third person, which is how free look has always behaved. */
46:         BOTH,
47:         /** Only with the camera behind the player. */
48:         FIRST,
49:         /** Only with the camera in front of the player. */
50:         THIRD
51:     }
52: 
53:     /** Largest free-look pitch offset, in degrees. Past this the world would start to invert. */
54:     private static final float MAX_PITCH = 90.0F;
55: 
56:     /** Time constant for easing the camera back onto the body, in seconds. */
57:     private static final double RETURN_SECONDS = 0.09D;
58: 
59:     /** Below this an offset snaps to zero, so easing cannot leave a permanent sliver behind. */
60:     private static final float EPSILON = 0.01F;
61: 
62:     /** Multiplier vanilla's {@code Entity.setAngles} applies to raw mouse deltas. */
63:     private static final float VANILLA_GAIN = 0.15F;
64: 
65:     private static Mode mode = Mode.HOLD;
66: 
67:     /** Which view the bind is allowed to work in. */
